{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nChange 1275 (ticket f1eb-5b53-f8bd-4f2b, \"Shell-to-Python Tier 2: probe-rebar.sh\nwith assertion-parity review\") ported the golden-path probe to\nscripts/probe_rebar.py and re-pointed every consumer, but the Gerrit\nVerified gate executes gerrit-verify.yaml from MAIN's workflow definition\nagainst the patchset tree — so the change had to keep a transitional\nscripts/probe-rebar.sh exec shim for main's still-shell golden-path step\nto invoke (patchset 1 failed golden-path with exit 127).\n\nChange 1275 has since merged. Verified on origin/main @ c3fb869ab5:\n- .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:209 → `run: python scripts/probe_rebar.py </dev/null`\n- .github/workflows/test.yml:128 → `run: python scripts/probe_rebar.py </dev/null`\n- tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py:45 asserts on `scripts/probe_rebar.py`\n- docs/releasing.md:401,405,407 → `python scripts/probe_rebar.py`\nThe shim therefore has zero invoking callers; only historical prose names it.\n\n## Plan\nDelete scripts/probe-rebar.sh. Nothing else changes — this is a pure removal\nwith no behavioral change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] scripts/probe-rebar.sh removed from the tree\n- [ ] No workflow, script, doc, or test *invokes* probe-rebar.sh. Proving command\n  (must print nothing):\n  `git grep -n 'probe-rebar' -- . ':!CHANGELOG.md' ':!pyproject.toml' ':!docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/operator_attested_ac_corpus.jsonl'`\n  The three excluded paths are known-benign historical residue, NOT invocations,\n  and are deliberately out of scope:\n  - CHANGELOG.md — release history, immutable by convention.\n  - pyproject.toml:445 — the comment \"(ticket f1eb, port of probe-rebar.sh)\" is an\n    accurate statement about where probe_rebar.py came from; rewriting it would\n    erase provenance, not fix a reference.\n  - docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/operator_attested_ac_corpus.jsonl:97 —\n    a FROZEN experiment corpus record of a past ticket's AC text; editing it would\n    corrupt the dataset.\n  (scripts/probe_rebar.py's own docstring says \"port of probe-rebar.sh\" — same\n  provenance rationale; it is covered by the deletion-only scope and left as-is.)\n- [ ] gerrit-verify golden-path job green on the deleting change itself\n  (proves main's definition no longer needs the shim)\n\n## File impact\n- scripts/probe-rebar.sh (delete)"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785892046725442001,"uuid":"d401401e-60a0-4ec2-9a7d-367a34903a03"}